# The scaffold runs on the clock-tower's chimes, one per turn, and
# the darkness does not exist until the THIRD chime brings it
# ("Darkness sways into vision just beside you"). The walkthroughs
# reach that beat on a different turn-count than this command
# sequence does, so their jump aimed at a darkness not yet born --
# four silent refusals in a row. One wait re-synchronizes the
# timeline. The window is two chimes wide; at the fifth the game
# shoves you through regardless, which is why the examine-dust turn
# below doubles as the stumble into the Empty Room, where the dust
# has been waiting all along.

wait
examine darkness
jump into the darkness
examine dust
blow dust


# The iron key falls through the window slot on a schedule -- four
# turns after arrival, heralded by footsteps and Antonio's voice --
# and the walkthroughs grab for it on turn one. The grabs fail
# silently, and the story punishes the desync twenty scenes later
# with an arrest. Played in intent order, the bottle-and-ropes work
# consumes exactly the turns the schedule needs, and the key is
# waiting when the hands are free.

