# The kill. Bare hands are refused -- "there are cleaner methods,
# there is your reputation to consider" -- because this assassin
# has never needed a weapon: the ring that marked its wearer for
# the scaffold goes onto Giuseppe's bound finger, the knock brings
# the old man's "Is it done?", and the darkness splits you in two:
# Sebastian DeLosa walks out free while an eye-and-ear stays to
# watch. The hanging that opened this game was never yours. The
# final scene is the crowd below the scaffold, Francesca's venom,
# and the epitaph: "An assassin, such as yourself -- you have no
# need of weapons."

remove ring
put ring on giuseppe
